{"source_sha256":"ed2869946b0de9d97398c975a3dde8d5701250eb4c8776cb40907fe23c6300bb","page_number":20,"page_type":"mixed","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b1","text":"Names: Hestia, Basil, Rune, Prism, Ember, Quintess, Aludel, Mordant, Salaman, Jazia","bbox":[36.0,551.08,347.26,573.85]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b2","text":"You are an artisan of the arcane, a smith of subtle forces. In the crucible of your workshop, the laws that govern this world are warped to suit your needs.","bbox":[36.0,86.08,353.1,108.85]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b3","text":"Starting Gear","bbox":[36.0,114.3,107.58,129.53]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b4","text":"• 3d6 Gold Pieces","bbox":[40.5,131.7,112.75,143.47]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b5","text":"• Rations (3 uses)","bbox":[40.5,144.7,110.91,156.47]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b6","text":"• Lantern","bbox":[40.5,157.7,80.7,169.47]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b7","text":"• Oil Can (6 uses)","bbox":[40.5,170.7,110.79,182.47]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b8","text":"• Needle-Knife (d6)","bbox":[40.5,183.7,119.6,195.47]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b9","text":"• Protective Gloves ( petty )","bbox":[40.5,196.7,146.01,208.58]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b10","text":"Aurifex","bbox":[36.0,42.54,149.54,86.86]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-20-b11","text":"BACKGROUND 1","bbox":[38.0,27.82,102.07,38.9]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-player-20-b11","a-cairn-player-20-b10","a-cairn-player-20-b2","a-cairn-player-20-b3","a-cairn-player-20-b4","a-cairn-player-20-b5","a-cairn-player-20-b6","a-cairn-player-20-b7","a-cairn-player-20-b8","a-cairn-player-20-b9","a-cairn-player-20-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-player-20-1","block_id":"a-cairn-player-20-b10","level":1},{"id":"h-cairn-player-20-2","block_id":"a-cairn-player-20-b3","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"ed2869946b0de9d97398c975a3dde8d5701250eb4c8776cb40907fe23c6300bb","page_number":30,"page_type":"mixed","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b1","text":"Names: Seed, Thresh, Dibber, Sow, Stalk, Harrow, Cobb, Flax, Briar, Rye","bbox":[36.0,562.08,317.89,573.85]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b2","text":"Protectors of the harvest, defense against pests, thieves, and beasts. A position of great honor, while it lasts: many guardians do not live out their natural lives.","bbox":[36.0,86.08,359.07,108.85]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b3","text":"Roll a second time on the Bonds table.","bbox":[36.0,112.58,186.91,124.35]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b4","text":"Starting Gear","bbox":[36.0,129.8,107.58,145.03]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b5","text":"• 3d6 Gold Pieces","bbox":[40.5,147.2,112.75,158.97]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b6","text":"• Rations (3 uses)","bbox":[40.5,160.2,110.91,171.97]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b7","text":"• Torch (3 uses)","bbox":[40.5,173.2,105.15,184.97]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b8","text":"• Brigandine (1 Armor, bulky )","bbox":[40.5,186.2,155.31,198.08]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b9","text":"• Sling (d6)","bbox":[40.5,199.2,86.3,210.97]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b10","text":"• Hand Axe (d6)","bbox":[40.5,212.2,104.84,223.97]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b11","text":"• Repellent (pick the type, 3 uses)","bbox":[40.5,225.2,174.6,236.97]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b12","text":"Fieldwarden","bbox":[36.0,42.54,225.73,86.86]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-30-b13","text":"BACKGROUND 6","bbox":[38.0,27.82,103.42,38.9]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-player-30-b13","a-cairn-player-30-b12","a-cairn-player-30-b2","a-cairn-player-30-b3","a-cairn-player-30-b4","a-cairn-player-30-b5","a-cairn-player-30-b6","a-cairn-player-30-b7","a-cairn-player-30-b8","a-cairn-player-30-b9","a-cairn-player-30-b10","a-cairn-player-30-b11","a-cairn-player-30-b1"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-player-30-1","block_id":"a-cairn-player-30-b12","level":1},{"id":"h-cairn-player-30-2","block_id":"a-cairn-player-30-b4","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"ed2869946b0de9d97398c975a3dde8d5701250eb4c8776cb40907fe23c6300bb","page_number":62,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b1","text":"Core Rules","bbox":[36.0,33.84,139.48,61.54]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b2","text":"Attributes Each of the three attributes are used in different circumstances. (see Saves.)","bbox":[36.0,70.65,337.29,97.32]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b3","text":"Saves","bbox":[36.0,209.66,68.2,226.28]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b4","text":"• A save is a roll to avoid negative outcomes from risky choices. Characters roll a d20 and compare the results to the appropriate attribute. If they roll equal to or under that attribute, they succeed. Otherwise, they fail. A 1 is always a success, and a 20 is always a failure.","bbox":[40.5,229.06,356.22,273.84]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b5","text":"• If two opponents are each trying to overcome the other, whoever is most at risk should save.","bbox":[40.5,277.56,350.97,300.34]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b6","text":"• If two characters need to take an action together, whoever is most at risk should save (usually the character with the lowest relevant Attribute).","bbox":[40.5,304.06,341.33,326.84]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b7","text":"Healing & Recovery","bbox":[36.0,334.56,147.74,351.18]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b8","text":"• Resting for a few moments and having a drink of water restores lost HP but may leave the party exposed. Bandages can stabilize a character that has taken Critical Damage.","bbox":[40.5,353.96,362.26,387.74]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b9","text":"• Attribute loss (see Critical Damage) can usually be restored with a week’s rest, facilitated by a healer or other appropriate source of expertise.","bbox":[40.5,391.46,359.55,414.24]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b10","text":"• Some healing services are free, while magical or more expedient means of recovery may come at a cost.","bbox":[40.5,417.96,343.4,440.74]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b11","text":"Deprivation & Fatigue","bbox":[36.0,448.46,161.44,465.08]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b12","text":"• A PC that lacks a crucial need (such as food or rest) is Deprived. Anyone Deprived for more than a day adds Fatigue to their inventory, one for each day. A Deprived PC cannot recover HP, Attributes, or item slots from Fatigue.","bbox":[40.5,467.86,353.91,501.64]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b13","text":"• A PC may also be forced to add Fatigue after casting spells or due to events occurring in the fiction. Each Fatigue occupies one slot and lasts until the PC is able to recuperate (such as with a full night’s rest in a safe spot).","bbox":[40.5,505.36,355.28,539.14]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b14","text":"• If a character is forced to add Fatigue to their inventory but they have no free slots, they must drop an item from their inventory.","bbox":[40.5,542.86,357.94,565.64]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b15","text":"Strength (STR)","bbox":[36.0,115.68,106.45,129.53]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b16","text":"Used for saves requiring physical power, like lifting gates, bending bars, resisting poison, etc.","bbox":[36.0,130.69,134.22,186.46]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b17","text":"Dexterity (DEX)","bbox":[148.5,115.68,223.54,129.53]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b18","text":"Used for saves requiring poise, speed, reflexes, dodging, climbing, sneaking, balancing, etc.","bbox":[148.5,130.69,246.72,175.46]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-62-b19","text":"Willpower (WIL) Used for saves to persuade, deceive, interrogate, intimidate, charm, provoke, manipulate spells, etc.","bbox":[261.0,115.68,355.11,184.12]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-player-62-b1","a-cairn-player-62-b2","a-cairn-player-62-b15","a-cairn-player-62-b17","a-cairn-player-62-b19","a-cairn-player-62-b16","a-cairn-player-62-b18","a-cairn-player-62-b3","a-cairn-player-62-b4","a-cairn-player-62-b5","a-cairn-player-62-b6","a-cairn-player-62-b7","a-cairn-player-62-b8","a-cairn-player-62-b9","a-cairn-player-62-b10","a-cairn-player-62-b11","a-cairn-player-62-b12","a-cairn-player-62-b13","a-cairn-player-62-b14"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-player-62-1","block_id":"a-cairn-player-62-b1","level":1},{"id":"h-cairn-player-62-2","block_id":"a-cairn-player-62-b2","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-player-62-3","block_id":"a-cairn-player-62-b3","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-player-62-4","block_id":"a-cairn-player-62-b7","level":2},{"id":"h-cairn-player-62-5","block_id":"a-cairn-player-62-b11","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"ed2869946b0de9d97398c975a3dde8d5701250eb4c8776cb40907fe23c6300bb","page_number":66,"page_type":"text-native","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b1","text":"Scars","bbox":[36.0,33.84,88.1,61.54]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b2","text":"If damage to a PC would reduce their HP to exactly 0, look up the result on the table below based on the amount of HP lost in the attack. For example, if a PC went from 3 HP to 0 HP, they would look at entry #3 (Walloped).","bbox":[36.0,66.65,348.9,100.42]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b3","text":"How much HP did you lose?","bbox":[142.7,111.12,253.3,122.89]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b4","text":"1 HP Lasting Scar: Roll 1d6 | 1: Neck, 2: Hands, 3: Eye, 4: Chest, 5: Legs, 6: Ear. Roll 1d6. If the total is higher than your max HP, take the new result.","bbox":[45.54,133.52,345.56,155.6]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b5","text":"2 HP Rattling Blow: You’re disoriented and shaken. Describe how you refocus. Roll 1d6. If the total is higher than your max HP, take the new result.","bbox":[45.03,165.92,351.06,188.0]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b6","text":"3 HP Walloped: You’re sent flying and land flat on your face, winded. You are deprived until you rest for a few hours. Then, roll 1d6. Add that amount to your max HP.","bbox":[44.92,197.04,353.39,230.12]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b7","text":"4 HP Broken Limb: Roll 1d6 | 1-2: Leg, 3-4: Arm, 5: Rib, 6: Skull. Once mended, roll 2d6. If the total is higher than your max HP, take the new result.","bbox":[44.98,239.16,346.55,261.24]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b8","text":"5 HP Diseased: You’re afflicted with a gross, uncomfortable infection. When you get over it, roll 2d6. If the total is higher than your max HP, take the new result.","bbox":[45.0,270.29,346.64,303.37]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b9","text":"6 HP Reorienting Head Wound: Roll 1d6 | 1-2: STR, 3-4: DEX, 5-6: WIL. Roll 3d6. If the total is higher than your current attribute, take the new result.","bbox":[44.86,312.41,354.94,334.49]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b10","text":"7 HP Hamstrung: You can barely move until you get serious help and rest. After recovery, roll 3d6. If the total is higher than your max DEX, take the new result.","bbox":[45.29,343.54,356.22,376.62]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b11","text":"8 HP Deafened: You cannot hear anything until you find extraordinary aid. Regardless, make a WIL save. If you pass, increase your max WIL by 1d4.","bbox":[44.88,385.66,344.23,407.74]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b12","text":"9 HP Re-brained: Some hidden part of your psyche is knocked loose. Roll 3d6. If the total is higher than your max WIL, take the new result.","bbox":[44.86,418.06,349.43,440.14]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b13","text":"10 HP Sundered: An appendage is torn off, crippled, or useless (the Warden will tell you which.) Then make a WIL save. If you pass, increase your max WIL by 1d6.","bbox":[43.0,449.18,354.93,482.26]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b14","text":"11 HP Mortal Wound: You are deprived and out of action. You die in one hour unless healed. Upon recovery, roll 2d6. Take the new result as your max HP.","bbox":[43.92,490.03,346.26,523.11]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-66-b15","text":"12 HP Doomed: Death seemed ever so close, but somehow you survived. If your next save against Critical Damage is a fail, you die horribly. If you pass, roll 3d6. If the total is higher than your max HP, take the new result.","bbox":[43.41,530.88,355.95,563.96]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-player-66-b1","a-cairn-player-66-b2","a-cairn-player-66-b3","a-cairn-player-66-b4","a-cairn-player-66-b5","a-cairn-player-66-b6","a-cairn-player-66-b7","a-cairn-player-66-b8","a-cairn-player-66-b9","a-cairn-player-66-b10","a-cairn-player-66-b11","a-cairn-player-66-b12","a-cairn-player-66-b13","a-cairn-player-66-b14","a-cairn-player-66-b15"],"headings":[{"id":"h-cairn-player-66-1","block_id":"a-cairn-player-66-b1","level":2}]}
{"source_sha256":"ed2869946b0de9d97398c975a3dde8d5701250eb4c8776cb40907fe23c6300bb","page_number":75,"page_type":"mixed","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b1","text":"Path Type","bbox":[107.45,39.09,154.64,52.94]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b2","text":"Path Penalty Odds of Getting Lost","bbox":[40.0,61.24,222.09,72.32]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b3","text":"Roads None None","bbox":[40.0,80.98,192.62,92.06]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b4","text":"Trails +1 Watch 2-in-6","bbox":[40.0,100.73,194.56,111.81]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b5","text":"Wilderness +2 Watches 3-in-6","bbox":[40.0,120.48,194.64,131.56]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b6","text":"Path Distance","bbox":[267.66,39.09,332.83,52.94]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b7","text":"Distance Penalty","bbox":[244.48,61.24,333.14,72.32]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b8","text":"Short +1 Watch","bbox":[244.48,80.98,337.73,92.06]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b9","text":"Medium +2 Watches","bbox":[244.48,100.73,347.15,111.81]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b10","text":"Long +3 Watches","bbox":[244.48,120.48,347.31,131.56]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b11","text":"Terrain Difficulty","bbox":[157.22,150.42,238.79,164.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b12","text":"Difficulty Terrain Penalty Factors","bbox":[40.5,175.76,252.56,186.84]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b13","text":"Easy Plains, plateaus, valleys None Safe areas for rest, fellow travelers, good visibility","bbox":[40.5,196.17,356.91,218.25]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b14","text":"Tough Forests, deserts, hills +1 Watch","bbox":[40.5,229.72,204.31,251.8]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b15","text":"Wild animals, flooding, broken equipment, falling rocks, unsafe shelters, hunter’s traps","bbox":[224.1,224.22,344.36,257.3]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b16","text":"Perilous Mountains, jungles, swamps +2 Watches","bbox":[40.5,268.76,213.73,290.84]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-75-b17","text":"Quicksand, sucking mud, choking vines, unclean water, poisonous plants and animals, poor navigation","bbox":[224.1,263.26,355.51,296.34]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-player-75-b1","a-cairn-player-75-b6","a-cairn-player-75-b2","a-cairn-player-75-b7","a-cairn-player-75-b3","a-cairn-player-75-b8","a-cairn-player-75-b4","a-cairn-player-75-b9","a-cairn-player-75-b5","a-cairn-player-75-b10","a-cairn-player-75-b11","a-cairn-player-75-b12","a-cairn-player-75-b13","a-cairn-player-75-b15","a-cairn-player-75-b14","a-cairn-player-75-b17","a-cairn-player-75-b16"],"headings":[]}
{"source_sha256":"ed2869946b0de9d97398c975a3dde8d5701250eb4c8776cb40907fe23c6300bb","page_number":76,"page_type":"mixed","blocks":[{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b1","text":"Weather","bbox":[36.0,34.7,85.56,51.32]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b2","text":"Each day, the Warden should roll on the weather table for the appropriate season. If the “Extreme” weather result is rolled twice in a row, the weather turns to “Catastrophic.” A squall becomes a hurricane, a storm floods the valley, etc.","bbox":[36.0,54.1,362.14,87.88]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b3","text":"Weather Difficulty","bbox":[154.76,375.8,241.73,389.65]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b4","text":"Weather Effect Examples","bbox":[40.48,399.32,283.9,410.4]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b5","text":"Nice Favorable conditions for travel. Clear skies, sunny","bbox":[40.48,420.44,314.11,431.52]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b6","text":"Fair Favorable conditions for travel. Overcast, breezy","bbox":[40.48,440.19,310.09,451.27]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b7","text":"Unpleasant Add a Fatigue or add +1 watch. Gusting winds, rain showers, sweltering heat, chill air","bbox":[40.48,459.94,356.92,482.02]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b8","text":"Inclement Add a Fatigue or add +1 watch. Increase terrain difficulty by a step.","bbox":[40.48,490.69,230.81,512.77]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b9","text":"Thunderstorms, lightning, rain, muddy ground","bbox":[247.48,490.69,346.78,512.77]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b10","text":"Extreme Add a Fatigue and add +1 watch. Increase terrain difficulty by a step.","bbox":[40.48,521.44,230.81,543.52]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b11","text":"Blizzards, freezing winds, flooding, mud slides","bbox":[247.48,521.44,343.95,543.52]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b12","text":"Catastrophic Most parties cannot travel under these conditions.","bbox":[40.48,552.18,223.22,574.26]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b13","text":"Tornados, tidal waves, hurricane, volcanic eruption","bbox":[247.48,552.18,352.9,574.26]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b14","text":"Weather","bbox":[177.73,205.29,218.27,219.14]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b15","text":"d6 Spring Summer Fall Winter","bbox":[46.44,227.44,317.84,238.52]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b16","text":"1 Nice Nice Fair Fair","bbox":[49.5,247.18,304.78,258.26]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b17","text":"2 Fair Nice Fair Unpleasant","bbox":[48.99,266.93,332.63,278.01]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b18","text":"3 Fair Fair Unpleasant Inclement","bbox":[48.88,286.68,328.3,297.76]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b19","text":"4 Unpleasant Unpleasant Inclement Inclement","bbox":[48.93,306.43,328.3,317.51]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b20","text":"5 Inclement Inclement Inclement Extreme","bbox":[48.96,326.18,322.16,337.26]},{"id":"a-cairn-player-76-b21","text":"6 Extreme Extreme Extreme Extreme","bbox":[48.82,345.92,322.16,357.0]}],"reading_order":["a-cairn-player-76-b1","a-cairn-player-76-b2","a-cairn-player-76-b14","a-cairn-player-76-b15","a-cairn-player-76-b16","a-cairn-player-76-b17","a-cairn-player-76-b18","a-cairn-player-76-b19","a-cairn-player-76-b20","a-cairn-player-76-b21","a-cairn-player-76-b3","a-cairn-player-76-b4","a-cairn-player-76-b5","a-cairn-player-76-b6","a-cairn-player-76-b7","a-cairn-player-76-b8","a-cairn-player-76-b9","a-cairn-player-76-b10","a-cairn-player-76-b11","a-cairn-player-76-b12","a-cairn-player-76-b13"],"headings":[]}
